# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — WindTurbineProject (Stanford PAI Final Project)
# Public GitHub repository preparation
# =============================================================================

# --- Python virtual environments ---
.venv/
venv/

# --- Environment files ---
# Ignore all .env files, but keep a checked-in .env.example as a template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Byte-compiled / cached Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# --- pytest cache ---
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/

# --- OpenCode / agent skill caches (local tooling, not project source) ---
.opencode/
.agents/

# --- OS-generated files ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.lnk

# --- Jupyter / notebook checkpoints (disposable) ---
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# NOTE: Project notebooks (*.ipynb) are NOT excluded by default so that they can
# be published and reviewed. Only .ipynb_checkpoints/ is ignored. If a notebook
# is later confirmed disposable, add its path explicitly below.

# =============================================================================
# Third-party / licensed data (redistribution-restricted)
#
# The ERA5-derived CSVs are third-party reanalysis data retrieved from the
# Open-Meteo Historical Weather API. Open-Meteo API data are CC BY 4.0; the
# underlying ERA5 is a separate Copernicus product whose licence terms were
# NOT independently verified (see SOURCES.md). To avoid redistributing
# licensed third-party data in a public repo, the raw + processed CSVs are
# gitignored. Keep them locally; re-download with:
#   python -m src.data_loader --force   (optional re-download)
#   python -m src.data_processing
#
# Provenance + quality metadata (small, no data values) are kept and published.
# =============================================================================
data/raw/openmeteo_era5_cuxhaven_2015_2024.csv
data/processed/cuxhaven_era5_hourly_2015_2024_processed.csv

# =============================================================================
# Large regeneratable artifacts (kept locally; reproducible from source)
#
# scenarios.csv is regenerated by the Monte Carlo pipeline. It is large relative
# to summary statistics and derivable on demand, so it is gitignored.
# =============================================================================
results/tables/scenarios.csv
